# Keep the Docker build context small (and the image privacy-safe).
# Every file matched here is NOT shipped to the Docker daemon, so a
# fresh build no longer waltzes 3+ GB of venv / node_modules / customer
# CSVs across the wire.

# ---------- VCS + IDE ----------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.gitlab
.vscode
.idea
.claude

# ---------- Python local state ----------
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.venv
venv
env

# ---------- Node / webapp ----------
# The frontend has its own Dockerfile -- it shouldn't be in the backend
# build context at all.
webapp
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.vite

# ---------- Runtime / generated data (never bake into image) ----------
data
logs
**/logs
**/cache
demand_forecasting_pipeline/artifacts
recommended_order/output
recommended_order/file_storage
llm_analytics/cache

# ---------- Secrets (defence in depth -- gitignored too) ----------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# ---------- Dev-only scripts + tooling ----------
scripts/_*
**/test_*.py
**/tests
.dockerignore
Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
nginx.conf
README.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE
pyproject.toml
render.yaml
fly.toml
railway.toml

# ---------- macOS / Windows noise ----------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
